Context
  Asked whether skills should have been namespaced guile:repl:{server,eval,proxy}
  rather than dash-prefixed, and whether to plan a deeper refactor at 0.5 or 1.0.
  Then asked to document the process for review rather than just the outcome, and to
  widen the sample using the claude-skills GitHub topic.

Deviations
  The document answers the method question, not the refactor question. The refactor
  decision needs the numbers this produced and is better made in an issue against
  them than asserted here.

Considerations
  The topic sample is biased toward popular repositories and is stated as such. It is
  good enough for the question asked: a popular-biased sample that CONTRADICTS a
  convention is decisive, while one that agrees is only suggestive. It contradicted
  mine, which is why the N4 claim changed.

  Two of the three nesting repos did not print their nested paths under my grep,
  which required a literal skills/ segment. Not chased -- the one clear example was
  enough to establish the shape, and 'good enough' was the explicit instruction.

Timeline
  2026-09-29, nexus, claude 2.1.261, gh CLI, as dsp-dr. 1,382 skills sampled across
  10 repositories plus 31 upstream and 25 installed.
